search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(ProbeArgJit);
define
    paSrc;
    paOut;
    paCallee argument code={
        paOut = argument * 2;
        };
    paDrive code={
        paCallee(paSrc);
        };
    ;

paSrc = 4;  paOut = 0;
print "PA fire 1 setup : paSrc =" paSrc:;
testing(paDrive);
print "PA fire 1 result: paOut =" paOut " (want 8)":;

paSrc = 11; paOut = 0;
print "PA fire 2 setup : paSrc =" paSrc " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "PA fire 2 result: paOut =" paOut " (want 22)":;

paSrc = 7;  paOut = 0;
paDrive();
print "PA interpreted  : paOut =" paOut " (oracle -- want 14)":;
print "PA SENTINEL":;
stop();

probeArgJit -- does a JITTED body read an action's `argument` as the passed
field, or as the holder?  There is no such fixture in the tree; every jit
fixture reads globals.  Minimal delta from incant/jitJ6 (globals + testing +
jitRefire + a value read), plus one argument-taking callee so the emitted call
goes through jitBindArgRT.

Jitted half FIRST, oracle LAST (bear-trap #25): an interpreted run consumes
isCoded and testing() would silently reroute to jitRunIfTest.  The oracle reads
a FIELD, which is correct in that position; only a RETURNED value needs its own
process (bear-trap #35).

    8 then 22, oracle 14      the jitted body reads the passed field per fire
    two fires the same        the value was folded, not loaded per fire
    0 / wrong / degrade > 0   the jitted body is not reading the passed field
